│ patch_description        │ The current program achieves a combined score of 0.85 with validation accuracy of 0.89    │
│                          │ and test accuracy of 0.87. Analysis of the prior program shows that using parametrized    │
│                          │ controlled rotations (CRY, CRZ) with strategic entanglement patterns achieved a score of  │
│                          │ 0.78, but with better test accuracy (0.88) despite lower validation accuracy.             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key observations:                                                                         │
│                          │ 1. The current ansatz uses only fixed CZ gates for entanglement, which may limit          │
│                          │ expressiveness                                                                            │
│                          │ 2. The prior program used parametrized controlled rotations (CRY, CRZ) which provided     │
│                          │ adaptive entanglement                                                                     │
│                          │ 3. Parameter efficiency is low (0.01), suggesting we could benefit from more strategic    │
│                          │ parameter use                                                                             │
│                          │ 4. The generalization gap is consistent at 0.07, indicating the model generalizes         │
│                          │ reasonably well                                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Strategy:                                                                                 │
│                          │ - Replace some fixed CZ gates with parametrized controlled rotations (CRY, CRZ) to enable │
│                          │ adaptive entanglement                                                                     │
│                          │ - Use parameter sharing strategically: share parameters across symmetric qubit pairs to   │
│                          │ reduce parameter count while maintaining expressiveness                                   │
│                          │ - Implement a two-layer entanglement pattern: even-indexed pairs with CRY, then           │
│                          │ odd-indexed pairs with CRZ                                                                │
│                          │ - This balances expressiveness with parameter efficiency and should improve test accuracy │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The new ansatz will:                                                                      │
│                          │ 1. Keep local RY rotations on all qubits                                                  │
│                          │ 2. Add a pre-entanglement RZ layer                                                        │
│                          │ 3. Use parametrized CRY gates on even pairs (0-1, 2-3, 4-5, 6-7) with shared parameters   │
│                          │ 4. Use parametrized CRZ gates on odd pairs (1-2, 3-4, 5-6) with shared parameters         │
│                          │ 5. Add a final RZ layer for phase adjustment                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This approach combines the benefits of the prior program's adaptive entanglement with     │
│                          │ improved parameter efficiency through sharing.                                            │
