│ patch_name               │ enhanced_entanglement_with_parameter_sharing                                              │
│ patch_description        │ Analysis of prior programs shows:                                                         │
│                          │ 1. Program 1 (score 0.78): Uses CRY/CRZ parametrized controlled rotations with            │
│                          │ independent parameters per pair, achieving 88% test accuracy but with high generalization │
│                          │ gap (0.07) and lower validation accuracy (0.85).                                          │
│                          │ 2. Program 2 (score 0.85): Uses a simpler linear chain of CZ gates with independent RY/RZ │
│                          │ pre/post rotations, achieving 87% test accuracy with better validation accuracy (0.89)    │
│                          │ and lower test loss (0.47).                                                               │
│                          │ 3. Current program (score 0.80): Has 116 parameters but shows a larger generalization gap │
│                          │ (0.10), suggesting overfitting despite fewer parameters.                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key observations:                                                                         │
│                          │ - Program 2's higher validation accuracy (0.89 vs 0.88) and lower validation loss (0.46   │
│                          │ vs 0.48) suggest better regularization through simpler, more structured entanglement.     │
│                          │ - The current program uses mixed fixed CZ and parametrized CRY gates, but the CRY gates   │
│                          │ may not be well-optimized.                                                                │
│                          │ - Parameter sharing can improve generalization by reducing degrees of freedom while       │
│                          │ maintaining expressiveness.                                                               │
│                          │ - Adding more structured two-qubit entanglement (like full-chain CZ patterns) helps       │
│                          │ information flow across qubits.                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Proposed improvement:                                                                     │
│                          │ 1. Expand the fixed CZ entanglement to cover more pairs (full chain + reverse chain) for  │
│                          │ better information propagation.                                                           │
