╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ enhance_entanglement_with_controlled_rotations                                            │
│ patch_description        │ The current program (score 0.85) uses a mix of parameter-shared single-qubit rotations,   │
│                          │ nearest-neighbor CRY gates, and some long-range CRY gates. However, there's room for      │
│                          │ improvement:                                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Analysis of prior programs**:                                                        │
│                          │    - The second prior program (score 0.85) used a full linear chain of CZ gates (all 7    │
│                          │ pairs) plus post-entanglement RZ layers, achieving 0.87 test accuracy.                    │
│                          │    - The current program (score 0.85) has only 6 CZ gates (next-nearest-neighbor) and 2   │
│                          │ long-range CRY gates, with 110 params.                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Key observations**:                                                                  │
│                          │    - The second prior program had higher test accuracy (0.87 vs 0.87 current) but more    │
│                          │ parameters (146) and depth (99 vs 105).                                                   │
│                          │    - The current program converges faster (540 vs 750 steps) but has slightly lower       │
│                          │ validation accuracy (0.86 vs 0.89).                                                       │
│                          │    - Parameter sharing in the current program helps reduce parameters but may limit       │
│                          │ expressiveness.                                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Proposed improvement**:                                                              │
│                          │    - Replace the next-nearest-neighbor CZ layer with a more comprehensive entanglement    │
│                          │ strategy.                                                                                 │
│                          │    - Add controlled single-qubit rotations (CRZ) between qubits to create finer-grained,  │
│                          │ learnable two-qubit interactions.                                                         │
│                          │    - Reduce parameter sharing on the single-qubit gates (rx_even/odd, rz_even/odd) to     │
│                          │ increase model expressiveness while keeping total parameters reasonable.                  │
│                          │    - Reorganize the circuit to alternate between strong entanglement and local feature    │
│                          │ refinement more effectively.                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 4. **Expected impact**:                                                                   │
│                          │    - Higher validation accuracy through better two-qubit interaction learning.            │
│                          │    - Maintain or improve test accuracy by better capturing data structure.                │
│                          │    - Potentially reduce the train-test gap through more balanced learning capacity.       │
│                          │    - Convergence should remain fast due to optimized gate ordering.                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The new design:                                                                           │
│                          │ - Keeps 8 individual RX gates (removes parameter sharing to gain expressiveness).         │
│                          │ - Improves entanglement with learnable CRZ gates on carefully chosen pairs.               │
│                          │ - Uses individual RY and RZ gates for better feature extraction.                          │
│                          │ - Reduces total parameter count moderately while improving quality.                       │
