│ patch_description        │ Adopt a hybrid approach combining program 2's proven pre/post RZ + CZ architecture with   │
│                          │ strategic parameter sharing to improve validation accuracy while keeping parameters       │
│                          │ efficient.                                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Program 2 achieved better validation accuracy (0.89) with a cleaner architecture (pre-RZ  │
│                          │ layer, nearest-neighbor CZ, post-RZ layer). The current design's aggressive parameter     │
│                          │ sharing and long-range entanglement may be overfitting despite having fewer parameters.   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This proposal:                                                                            │
│                          │ 1. Returns to the pre/post RZ sandwich structure with CZ nearest-neighbor gates (proven   │
│                          │ effective)                                                                                │
│                          │ 2. Adds selective parameter sharing only where it's beneficial (RY layers share within    │
│                          │ even/odd groups for efficiency)                                                           │
│                          │ 3. Removes problematic long-range CRY gates which add depth without proven benefit        │
│                          │ 4. Balances model capacity and generalization                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Expected improvements:                                                                    │
│                          │ - Higher validation accuracy (targeting 0.89+)                                            │
│                          │ - Better generalization (lower gen gap)                                                   │
│                          │ - Slightly more parameters than current but better accuracy/parameter trade-off           │
│                          │ - Faster convergence due to cleaner architecture                                          │
