                        Patch Metadata - Gen 10/100 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 2/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ full_block_recycling_via_ansatz                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ Since we can only modify ANSATZ_SPEC within the EVOLVE-BLOCK, we achieve full block       │
│                          │ parameter recycling by designing the ansatz to use a minimal, highly-shared parameter set │
│                          │ that will naturally recycle across all 6 block applications (3 uploads × 2 repeats).      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Key insight:** The fixed training loop multiplies N_CIRCUIT_PARAMS = N_PARAMS_PER_BLOCK │
│                          │ × N_UPLOADS × N_REPEATS. By creating an ANSATZ_SPEC with very few unique parameter names  │
│                          │ (ideally just 1-2 shared across all gates), we force the system to reuse the same         │
│                          │ parameters across all block instances.                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Strategy:**                                                                             │
│                          │ - Use a single shared parameter name (e.g., "theta") for all parametrized gates in the    │
│                          │ ansatz block                                                                              │
│                          │ - This makes N_PARAMS_PER_BLOCK = 1, so N_CIRCUIT_PARAMS = 1 × 3 × 2 = 6 total circuit    │
│                          │ parameters                                                                                │
│                          │ - Combined with 2 readout parameters, N_PARAMS = 8 total                                  │
│                          │ - This extreme parameter sharing echoes the success of prior program 2 (68 params) and    │
│                          │ should dramatically improve parameter_efficiency                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Expected benefits:**                                                                    │
│                          │ 1. Massive parameter reduction (from 110 to 8 total)                                      │
│                          │ 2. Extreme regularization preventing overfitting                                          │
│                          │ 3. Fast convergence due to tiny parameter space                                           │
│                          │ 4. High parameter_efficiency metric (test_accuracy / N_PARAMS)                            │
│                          │ 5. Simpler optimization landscape for Adam                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This is a conservative, minimal-parameter design that tests whether the fixed IsingZZ     │
│                          │ feature uploads provide sufficient expressivity on their own.                             │
