│ patch_description        │ Since N_REPEATS and N_UPLOADS are fixed outside the EVOLVE-BLOCK and cannot be modified,  │
│                          │ I must increase depth by enriching the ANSATZ_SPEC itself. The current program achieves   │
│                          │ depth=126 with only 4 unique parameters (ry_0..7 shared, rz_pre/post shared, cry_a)       │
│                          │ across 68 total params.                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The strategy is to add more parametrized two-qubit entangling gates to create richer      │
│                          │ correlations while keeping parameter count reasonable. Specifically:                      │
│                          │ 1. Add additional CRZ layers with different control-target pairs to increase non-local    │
│                          │ interactions                                                                              │
│                          │ 2. Add CRX gates to complement the existing CRY gates                                     │
│                          │ 3. Extend the post-RZ layer or add intermediate RY rotations for more expressive power    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This will increase circuit depth to ~150-160 (closer to the recommended 135+) while using │
│                          │ efficient parameter sharing. The recommendation emphasizes that depths ≥90 correlated     │
│                          │ with top performance, and the current depth=126 suggests room for improvement. By adding  │
│                          │ structured entanglement without excessive parameter bloat, we test whether this reaches   │
│                          │ the performance ceiling around test_accuracy≈0.90.                                        │
