│ patch_description        │ The current program achieves 0.84 combined score with test accuracy of 0.85, but shows a  │
│                          │ notable generalization gap of 0.10 (train 0.95 vs test 0.85). The prior programs          │
│                          │ demonstrate that strategic entanglement patterns can improve generalization:              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. The first seed (score 0.85) used a simple line of CZ gates with good generalization    │
│                          │ (gap 0.07).                                                                               │
│                          │ 2. The second program (score 0.85) added diagonal CZ couplings and parametrized CRY       │
│                          │ gates, achieving 0.85 test accuracy with gap 0.05.                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The current program has 164 parameters with CRZ gates in a line pattern, leading to       │
│                          │ overfitting (gap 0.10). The recommendation suggests alternating two CZ-chain patterns     │
│                          │ between blocks:                                                                           │
│                          │ - Odd blocks: CZ on (0,1), (2,3), (4,5), (6,7) — pairs of adjacent qubits                 │
│                          │ - Even blocks: CZ on (1,2), (3,4), (5,6) — staggered pairs                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This enriches entanglement connectivity without adding parametrized two-qubit gates,      │
│                          │ maintaining expressivity while reducing the parameter count and improving generalization. │
│                          │ The alternating pattern ensures all qubits are coupled across multiple pathways, which    │
│                          │ typically improves information flow and reduces overfitting.                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ I will:                                                                                   │
│                          │ 1. Replace the parametrized CRZ line with fixed CZ gates in an alternating pattern        │
│                          │ 2. Reduce the single-qubit RX gates (currently only on even wires) to all wires for       │
│                          │ better expressivity with fewer parameters                                                 │
│                          │ 3. Keep RY and RZ layers but ensure the overall parameter count is reasonable             │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
