├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ full_block_recycling_via_ansatz_spec                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The recommendation implements **full block parameter recycling** by designing the         │
│                          │ ANSATZ_SPEC to use a single, unified set of parameter names across all block instances.   │
│                          │ Since the fixed training loop calls `apply_ansatz_block()` six times (3 uploads × 2       │
│                          │ repeats), and each call uses the same ANSATZ_SPEC with the same parameter names, all six  │
│                          │ block instances will automatically share the same parameters.                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Motivation:**                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. The prior programs demonstrate that parameter sharing dramatically improves            │
│                          │ efficiency: the second program achieved 0.85 test accuracy with only 68 params (vs. 146   │
│                          │ in the seed), proving that sharing reduces overfitting.                                   │
│                          │ 2. The current program uses 110 circuit parameters spread across 6 block instances. By    │
│                          │ reusing a single parameter set, we reduce N_CIRCUIT_PARAMS from 108 to ~16, keeping only  │
│                          │ the block's unique parameters.                                                            │
│                          │ 3. The fixed IsingZZ feature map is re-applied at each upload, providing strong signal    │
│                          │ injection. The ansatz block's role is to process this signal; reusing parameters means    │
│                          │ the block learns more general transformations that are reinforced 6 times.                │
│                          │ 4. Benefits: (a) simpler optimization landscape, (b) each parameter receives gradient     │
│                          │ updates 6 times per epoch (amplified learning signal), (c) parameter sharing acts as      │
│                          │ regularization, reducing overfitting and generalization gap.                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Implementation:**                                                                       │
│                          │ Simplify ANSATZ_SPEC to use only 16 unique parameter names (no per-block or per-upload    │
│                          │ suffixes). The existing `apply_ansatz_block()` function will automatically reuse these    │
│                          │ parameters for all 6 block instances because it always looks up parameters by name in     │
│                          │ PARAMETER_KEYS_PER_BLOCK, which is derived from the ANSATZ_SPEC.                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Expected outcome:**                                                                     │
│                          │ - N_CIRCUIT_PARAMS reduced from 108 to 16 (single block's parameters).                    │
│                          │ - N_PARAMS reduced from 110 to 18 (16 circuit + 2 readout).                               │
│                          │ - Improved parameter efficiency (test_accuracy / n_params).                               │
│                          │ - Faster convergence due to amplified gradient signal.                                    │
│                          │ - Reduced generalization gap through regularization.                                      │
│                          │ - Maintained circuit depth and expressivity (still 6 block applications).                 │
