╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ multi_basis_entangling_ladder                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ This approach fundamentally differs from the current linear-chain CZ entanglement by      │
│                          │ introducing a **multi-basis hierarchical entanglement strategy**. Instead of treating all │
│                          │ qubits uniformly with independent single-qubit rotations followed by a fixed entangling   │
│                          │ chain, this design:                                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Sparse parametrization**: Uses only 3 unique shared parameters per block (one for    │
│                          │ each basis: X, Y, Z) that apply to all qubits of the same type, dramatically reducing     │
│                          │ parameter count from 24 to ~6 per block while maintaining expressivity through            │
│                          │ **controlled parameter reuse**.                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Hierarchical two-qubit interactions**: Replaces the simple linear chain with a       │
│                          │ **ladder topology** combining nearest-neighbor (0-1, 2-3, 4-5, 6-7) and skip-neighbor     │
│                          │ (1-3, 3-5, 5-7) CZ gates. This creates richer entanglement patterns without exponential   │
│                          │ gate overhead.                                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Asymmetric basis rotation order**: Applies rotations in XY→Z order (instead of       │
│                          │ YX→Z), which better exploits the IsingZZ feature encoding by allowing intermediate Z      │
│                          │ corrections to actively reshape the encoded phase information.                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 4. **Parameter sharing across qubits**: Pairs qubits share parameters (e.g., CRY on [0,4] │
│                          │ and [1,5] use the same angle), reducing the circuit size while encouraging correlated     │
│                          │ learning on distant qubits.                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Why this should perform better**:                                                       │
│                          │ - **Faster convergence**: 6 parameters vs. 24 per block means lower-dimensional           │
│                          │ optimization landscape; shared parameters act as implicit regularization.                 │
│                          │ - **Reduced generalization gap**: Fewer free parameters naturally fight overfitting; the  │
│                          │ 0.07 gap should tighten.                                                                  │
│                          │ - **Better expressivity-to-depth ratio**: Ladder entanglement reaches all qubits in fewer │
│                          │ steps than linear chains; hierarchical structure respects the 28-feature input structure  │
│                          │ (4 qubits × 7 feature pairs per qubit).                                                   │
│                          │ - **Improved parameter efficiency**: Combining sparsity with smarter connectivity should  │
│                          │ yield higher test_accuracy / n_params ratio.                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This is a fundamentally different **ansatz architecture**, not an incremental tuning of   │
│                          │ gates or parameter sharing.                                                               │
