                        Patch Metadata - Gen 16/100 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ alternating_cz_connectivity                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ The current program achieves a combined score of 0.85, while the second prior program     │
│                          │ achieves 0.90 with only 44 parameters and better test accuracy (0.90 vs 0.85). The key    │
│                          │ insight from the prior programs is that the second one uses aggressive parameter sharing  │
│                          │ (e.g., all RY gates share "ry_0", all RZ pre-gates share "rz_pre") combined with a more   │
│                          │ compact entanglement structure.                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The current program has 68 parameters with individual RY parameters per qubit (ry_0       │
│                          │ through ry_7), which increases parameter count without improving generalization. The      │
│                          │ recommendation suggests alternating CZ-chain patterns between blocks to broaden           │
│                          │ connectivity while keeping the circuit lean.                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The strategy is to:                                                                       │
│                          │ 1. Reduce parameter count by using parameter sharing for single-qubit rotations (like the │
│                          │ successful second prior program)                                                          │
│                          │ 2. Implement alternating CZ connectivity patterns: even-indexed blocks use                │
│                          │ nearest-neighbor chains (0-1, 2-3, 4-5, 6-7), while odd-indexed blocks use the current    │
│                          │ cross-chain pattern (0-2, 1-3, 2-4, 3-5, 4-6, 5-7)                                        │
│                          │ 3. Remove the parametrized CRY gates and replace with simpler fixed entanglement to       │
│                          │ reduce parameters                                                                         │
│                          │ 4. Keep the RZ post-layer for expressiveness                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This approach combines the parameter efficiency of the second prior program with the      │
│                          │ connectivity exploration suggested in the recommendation, aiming for test accuracy ≥0.90  │
│                          │ with better generalization.                                                               │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
