│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ alternating_cz_chain_rewiring                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ The current program uses extreme parameter sharing (single "theta" parameter) which       │
│                          │ achieves high parameter efficiency but sacrifices expressiveness and accuracy. The prior  │
│                          │ programs show that moderate parameter sharing with diverse gate types and strategic       │
│                          │ connectivity patterns yields better accuracy (0.90-0.92 test) while maintaining           │
│                          │ reasonable parameter counts (44-50 params).                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The recommendation suggests alternating CZ-chain rewiring: dynamically cycle the dense CZ │
│                          │ pattern across ansatz blocks to inject broader connectivity without adding gates. This    │
│                          │ builds on the rapid convergence of dense-CZ designs while improving expressiveness.       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The new approach:                                                                         │
│                          │ 1. Restore moderate parameter sharing (separate parameters for different qubit groups and │
│                          │ gate types) to improve expressiveness                                                     │
│                          │ 2. Implement alternating CZ connectivity: even-indexed blocks use standard                │
│                          │ nearest-neighbor + cross-block CZ, odd-indexed blocks shift the pattern by one qubit      │
│                          │ (modulo 8)                                                                                │
│                          │ 3. Add parametrized two-qubit gates (CRY, CRZ) for controlled entanglement                │
│                          │ 4. Maintain efficient parameter count (~40-45 params) while improving accuracy and        │
│                          │ reducing the train-test gap                                                               │
│                          │ 5. Use RX, RY, RZ rotations with strategic parameter sharing to balance expressiveness    │
│                          │ and efficiency                                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This design leverages the success of the prior programs while implementing the            │
│                          │ alternating connectivity recommendation to achieve better generalization and faster       │
│                          │ convergence.                                                                              │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
