                        Patch Metadata - Gen 26/100 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 2/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ mid_block_crz_enrichment                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ The current program achieves a combined score of 0.88 with validation loss of 0.38 and    │
│                          │ slow convergence at 270 steps. The prior programs show better performance (0.89-0.90      │
│                          │ scores) with faster convergence (120-180 steps).                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The key insight is to add a mid-block enrichment layer after the CZ chains but before the │
│                          │ long-range gates. Instead of IsingZZ (which requires external gate support), we use CRZ   │
│                          │ gates on strategically chosen qubit pairs to create additional controlled phase           │
│                          │ correlations.                                                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This approach:                                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Adds structured entanglement**: CRZ gates on mid-range pairs (0-3, 1-4, 2-5, 3-6,    │
│                          │ 4-7) create intermediate-range correlations that bridge local (nearest-neighbor) and      │
│                          │ long-range (0-4, 1-5, etc.) interactions.                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Efficient parameter sharing**: A single shared parameter "crz_mid" across all        │
│                          │ mid-block CRZ gates adds minimal overhead (1 parameter per block) while enriching         │
│                          │ expressiveness.                                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Accelerates convergence**: The structured intermediate entanglement helps the        │
│                          │ circuit learn feature interactions more efficiently, reducing convergence time from 270   │
│                          │ to ~150-180 steps.                                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 4. **Improves generalization**: Better intermediate structure reduces overfitting         │
│                          │ (generalization_gap from 0.04 to ~0.02).                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Expected improvements:                                                                    │
│                          │ - Reduce convergence_step from 270 to ~150-180                                            │
│                          │ - Reduce validation_loss from 0.38 to ~0.35-0.36                                          │
│                          │ - Improve test_accuracy from 0.90 to 0.91+                                                │
│                          │ - Better generalization (reduce gap from 0.04 to ~0.02)                                   │
│                          │ - Combined score from 0.88 to 0.91+                                                       │
