│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ adaptive_entanglement_ansatz                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ The current program achieves 0.87 combined score with 50 parameters but shows a           │
│                          │ validation-test gap of 0.04 (87% vs 88%), indicating overfitting. The prior programs      │
│                          │ achieved 0.89-0.90 with better generalization.                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key observations from prior programs:                                                     │
│                          │ 1. Program 1 (score 0.89): Used 50 params with even/odd RY/RZ sharing, nearest-neighbor   │
│                          │ CRY, and long-range CRY—achieved 90% test accuracy with only 0.01 gap.                    │
│                          │ 2. Program 2 (score 0.90): Used 44 params with more complex entanglement (CRY, CRZ, CRX   │
│                          │ on mid-range pairs)—achieved 90% test accuracy with 0.02 gap.                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Current program issues:                                                                   │
│                          │ - Uses CRZ for long-range (less expressive than CRY for this task)                        │
│                          │ - Only 2 long-range gates vs. prior's 4 parametrized mid-range gates                      │
│                          │ - Validation accuracy dropped to 87% (from 91-92% in priors)                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ New strategy:                                                                             │
│                          │ 1. Restore the even/odd parameter sharing pattern from Program 1 (proven effective)       │
│                          │ 2. Add mid-range parametrized entanglement (CRY on [0,4], [1,5], [2,6], [3,7]) like       │
│                          │ Program 2                                                                                 │
│                          │ 3. Keep nearest-neighbor CRY but with independent parameter                               │
│                          │ 4. Use RY/RZ with even/odd split for better expressivity                                  │
│                          │ 5. Target 40-45 parameters for efficiency while maintaining expressivity                  │
│                          │ 6. Reduce depth by removing redundant fixed CZ gates and focusing on parametrized gates   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This combines the best elements: Program 1's proven even/odd sharing + validation         │
│                          │ accuracy, with Program 2's mid-range entanglement strategy.                               │
