│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ hybrid_efficient_ansatz_crossover                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ This crossover combines the best aspects of three candidate implementations:              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **From the first prior program (score 0.91, 26 params)**: The highly efficient         │
│                          │ parameter-sharing strategy with only 5 unique parameters (ry_init, rz_main, cry_nnn,      │
│                          │ ry_final) and strong entanglement structure. This achieves excellent test accuracy (0.93) │
│                          │ with minimal parameters and good parameter efficiency (0.04).                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **From the current program (score 0.87, 50 params)**: The symmetric qubit pairing      │
│                          │ strategy (even/odd qubits) and the use of RX gates for initial rotations, which provides  │
│                          │ diverse rotation axes.                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **From the second prior program (score 0.90, 44 params)**: The balanced approach with  │
│                          │ moderate parameter sharing and good generalization.                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Key improvements in this crossover:**                                                   │
│                          │ - Adopts the highly efficient 5-parameter structure from the best performer (0.91 score)  │
│                          │ - Integrates the symmetric even/odd qubit pairing from the current program for better     │
│                          │ expressivity                                                                              │
│                          │ - Combines nearest-neighbor CZ ring (for local entanglement) with cross-ring CZ (for      │
│                          │ long-range) from the first prior                                                          │
│                          │ - Adds parametrized CRY gates on next-nearest-neighbor pairs for flexible entanglement    │
│                          │ - Maintains the proven final RY readout layer                                             │
│                          │ - Reduces total parameters to 26 (matching the best performer) while potentially          │
│                          │ improving generalization through better qubit symmetry                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This hybrid approach aims to achieve:                                                     │
│                          │ - High test accuracy (target ≥0.93)                                                       │
│                          │ - Excellent parameter efficiency (target ≥0.04)                                           │
│                          │ - Low generalization gap (target ≤0.01)                                                   │
│                          │ - Minimal validation loss (target ≤0.32)                                                  │
