                        Patch Metadata - Gen 31/100 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 2/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ enhance_ansatz_with_readout_layer                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ The current program scores 0.87 with validation accuracy of 0.87 and test accuracy of     │
│                          │ 0.88. The prior programs achieved 0.90 and 0.91 by incorporating per-wire readout         │
│                          │ calibration.                                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Since I cannot modify the circuit_z_expectations function or parameter initialization     │
│                          │ (they are outside EVOLVE-BLOCK), I will add explicit per-wire RY and RZ rotations at the  │
│                          │ end of the ANSATZ_SPEC itself. These rotations will:                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Provide per-wire phase calibration**: Each qubit gets individual RY and RZ rotations │
│                          │ with shared parameters, allowing the circuit to learn residual phase offsets.             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Work within existing framework**: By adding these gates to ANSATZ_SPEC, they are     │
│                          │ applied as part of each ansatz block (repeated 6 times across 3 uploads × 2 repeats),     │
│                          │ giving the optimizer multiple opportunities to learn effective calibration.               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Minimal parameter overhead**: Using only 2 shared parameter keys ("ry_readout" and   │
│                          │ "rz_readout") for all 8 qubits keeps the parameter count reasonable while providing       │
│                          │ significant expressiveness.                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 4. **Improve generalization**: The current generalization gap is 0.04; per-wire           │
│                          │ calibration should help align training and test performance by capturing systematic       │
│                          │ per-qubit biases.                                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This approach directly addresses the recommendation to add readout rotations and should   │
│                          │ improve validation accuracy, reduce the train-test gap, and enhance overall performance.  │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0567                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
