                        Patch Metadata - Gen 34/100 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 2/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ per_wire_readout_rotations                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ The current program achieves a combined score of 0.89, whereas the prior baseline         │
│                          │ achieved 0.91. The main performance gap appears in test accuracy (0.88 vs 0.93) and test  │
│                          │ loss (0.42 vs 0.34).                                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Analysis:**                                                                             │
│                          │ The prior program uses aggressive parameter sharing (3 unique keys across 8 qubits per    │
│                          │ block) and applies simple gain/bias calibration to the mean Z expectation. The current    │
│                          │ program has increased to 6 unique parameter keys but test performance has degraded. This  │
│                          │ suggests the extra parameters are not being used efficiently, and the readout mechanism   │
│                          │ is too simplistic to capture per-wire phase information.                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Proposed Improvement:**                                                                 │
│                          │ Following the formal recommendation, I will add per-wire variational readout rotations    │
│                          │ directly within ANSATZ_SPEC. These RY and RZ gates will be applied to all qubits at the   │
│                          │ end of each ansatz block using two new shared parameter keys ("ry_read" and "rz_read").   │
│                          │ This approach:                                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Uses only 2 additional shared parameter keys, adding minimal overhead.                 │
│                          │ 2. Captures residual per-wire phase offsets that the global gain/bias cannot correct.     │
│                          │ 3. Works synergistically with the existing global calibration: gain/bias handles the      │
│                          │ overall signal scale, while per-wire rotations correct per-qubit phase distortions.       │
│                          │ 4. Are applied within the ansatz block so they benefit from the full differentiation      │
│                          │ pipeline.                                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Expected Impact:**                                                                      │
│                          │ - Test accuracy should improve toward ~0.92–0.93 (reducing gap to prior baseline).        │
│                          │ - Test loss should improve toward ~0.35.                                                  │
│                          │ - Minimal increase in depth and gate count (16 single-qubit gates per block).             │
│                          │ - Parameter efficiency should remain reasonable since we only add 2 unique parameters per │
│                          │ block.                                                                                    │
