                        Patch Metadata - Gen 35/100 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 2/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ optimized_ansatz_fewer_params                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ The current program has 110 parameters with poor generalization (test accuracy 0.87, gap  │
│                          │ 0.04). The prior seed achieved 0.93 test accuracy with only 26 parameters using           │
│                          │ aggressive parameter sharing and a more compact structure.                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The current ANSATZ_SPEC has 18 unique parameters per block (2 shared RY + 8 individual RZ │
│                          │ pre + 8 individual RZ post), leading to 18 * 3 * 2 = 108 circuit parameters plus 2        │
│                          │ readout = 110 total.                                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The key insight: the prior seed used only 4 unique parameters per block (ry_init,         │
│                          │ rz_main, cry_nnn, ry_final) and achieved better accuracy. The current design with         │
│                          │ per-qubit RZ gates is over-parameterized and likely overfitting.                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Strategy:                                                                                 │
│                          │ 1. Reduce pre-entanglement RZ to use parameter sharing (like rz_pre for all qubits)       │
│                          │ 2. Reduce post-entanglement RZ to use parameter sharing (like rz_post for all qubits)     │
│                          │ 3. Keep the efficient nearest-neighbor CZ structure                                       │
│                          │ 4. This reduces unique parameters per block from 18 to 4, matching the prior architecture │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Expected outcome: Fewer parameters (26 total), better generalization, higher test         │
│                          │ accuracy closer to 0.93.                                                                  │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0690                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
