╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ enhanced_entanglement_pattern                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz achieves 0.93 test accuracy with 26 parameters. Analysis of prior      │
│                          │ programs shows:                                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. The first prior program (38 params, 0.90 test acc) had more complex entanglement but   │
│                          │ lower parameter efficiency.                                                               │
│                          │ 2. The second prior program (26 params, 0.93 test acc) balanced efficiency and accuracy   │
│                          │ with a clean next-nearest-neighbor (NNN) pattern.                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Improvement strategy:**                                                                 │
│                          │ - The current program uses full parameter sharing on RY gates (ry_init, ry_final), which  │
│                          │ is efficient but may limit expressivity.                                                  │
│                          │ - Add **per-qubit parametrized rotations** in the middle layer instead of shared          │
│                          │ parameters, giving the circuit more flexibility to encode different information on each   │
│                          │ qubit.                                                                                    │
│                          │ - Replace some of the 8 shared CRY gates (cry_nnn) with **individual CRY pairs on         │
│                          │ complementary qubit sets** to create richer entanglement patterns.                        │
│                          │ - Introduce **alternating RX and RY** in the initial layer to break symmetry and improve  │
│                          │ gradient flow.                                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This keeps the parameter count reasonable (~28-30 params per block, still better than 38) │
│                          │ while increasing expressivity through reduced parameter sharing and enhanced entanglement │
│                          │ connectivity.                                                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Key changes:**                                                                          │
│                          │ 1. Split ry_init into per-qubit parameters (ry_0, ry_1, ..., ry_7) for initial layer      │
│                          │ 2. Keep rz_main shared (efficiency)                                                       │
│                          │ 3. Enhance CRY coverage with additional cross-qubit connections                           │
│                          │ 4. Use selective parameter sharing in the final layer (alternating ry_final and           │
│                          │ ry_final_alt)                                                                             │
