│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ extend_nearest_neighbor_cry_entanglement                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ The current program achieves 0.89 combined score with 50 parameters and decent            │
│                          │ performance, but lags behind the seed programs (0.91 score with 26 parameters). The key   │
│                          │ insight from the recommendation is to extend parametrized entanglement patterns at zero   │
│                          │ parameter cost by reusing existing parameter keys.                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Currently, Layer 2 only applies CRY gates on pairs (0,1), (2,3), (4,5), (6,7) with the    │
│                          │ shared parameter `cry_nn`. The recommendation suggests adding nearest-neighbor pairs at   │
│                          │ zero cost by also applying CRY on the "wrap-around" pairs that complete the ring: (1,2),  │
│                          │ (3,4), (5,6), (7,0).                                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This doubles the nearest-neighbor entanglement connectivity without adding any new        │
│                          │ parameters (both old and new gates use the same `cry_nn` key). The expected benefits are: │
│                          │ 1. Richer mid-block expressivity through denser local correlations                        │
│                          │ 2. Better information flow across the qubit ring                                          │
│                          │ 3. Potential to reduce the number of unique parameters while maintaining or improving     │
│                          │ expressivity                                                                              │
│                          │ 4. The current parameter-heavy design (50 params) seems to overfit; enhanced entanglement │
│                          │ with the same param count might achieve better generalization                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This is a low-risk, high-potential improvement that directly addresses the asymmetry in   │
│                          │ the current entanglement pattern.                                                         │
