│ patch_description        │ The current program achieves a combined score of 0.88 with 20 parameters and relatively   │
│                          │ low accuracy (0.86 test). The prior programs achieved 0.91 with 26 parameters using a 3×2 │
│                          │ structure (3 uploads, 2 repeats).                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The recommendation suggests rebalancing to 2 uploads × 3 repeats, maintaining the same    │
│                          │ total of 6 variational blocks and similar parameter count, but testing whether fewer data │
│                          │ re-encodings with deeper intra-upload circuits converge faster or yield better accuracy.  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key changes:                                                                              │
│                          │ 1. Set N_UPLOADS = 2 and N_REPEATS = 3 (instead of 3 and 2)                               │
│                          │ 2. Expand the ANSATZ_SPEC to include richer entanglement patterns that can be repeated 3  │
│                          │ times per upload                                                                          │
│                          │ 3. Add more parametrized two-qubit gates (CRY, CRZ) to increase expressiveness within     │
│                          │ each repeat                                                                               │
│                          │ 4. Maintain efficient parameter sharing where appropriate                                 │
│                          │ 5. Keep total circuit depth and parameter count reasonable                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The new ansatz includes:                                                                  │
│                          │ - Initial RY basis rotation (shared)                                                      │
│                          │ - Nearest-neighbor CZ ring for local entanglement                                         │
│                          │ - Parametrized CRY gates on multiple qubit pairs for flexible entanglement                │
│                          │ - RZ phase rotations (shared)                                                             │
│                          │ - Additional CRZ gates for cross-qubit phase correlations                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This structure allows the circuit to learn more complex feature interactions with fewer   │
│                          │ data re-uploads, potentially improving convergence speed and generalization.              │
