│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ nearest_neighbor_cry_enrichment                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ The current program has 38 parameters per block and achieves a combined score of 0.90,    │
│                          │ while the prior programs with 26 parameters achieved 0.91. The recommendation suggests    │
│                          │ extending the mid-block CRY entangler to nearest neighbors at zero extra parameter cost   │
│                          │ by reusing the existing "cry_nnn" parameter key.                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Looking at the prior high-performance architecture (Gen 28 baseline), it achieves         │
│                          │ excellent results with:                                                                   │
│                          │ - Test accuracy: 0.93 (vs current 0.90)                                                   │
│                          │ - Parameter efficiency: 0.04 (vs current 0.02)                                            │
│                          │ - Only 26 total parameters (vs current 38)                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The key insight is that the current design (38 params) is over-parametrized relative to   │
│                          │ the problem complexity. The prior design uses parameter sharing more aggressively and     │
│                          │ includes next-nearest-neighbor CRY gates with a single shared parameter.                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The recommendation is to:                                                                 │
│                          │ 1. Simplify the ansatz to reduce parameter count                                          │
│                          │ 2. Add nearest-neighbor CRY gates (reusing "cry_nnn" parameter) to build richer           │
│                          │ connectivity without increasing parameter count                                           │
│                          │ 3. Restore the efficient multi-layer structure with aggressive parameter sharing          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This approach follows the proven pattern: smaller parameter count + smarter connectivity  │
│                          │ = better generalization and higher parameter efficiency.                                  │
