                        Patch Metadata - Gen 48/100 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_mid_ry_layer_before_entanglers                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ The current program (score 0.89) uses 50 parameters but achieves only 90% test accuracy   │
│                          │ with higher loss (0.44) compared to the seed baseline (0.91 score, 26 params, 93% test    │
│                          │ accuracy, 0.34 loss).                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Analysis:                                                                                 │
│                          │ 1. The current ansatz has too many parameters (50 vs 26) but lower accuracy, suggesting   │
│                          │ overfitting or inefficient parameter use.                                                 │
│                          │ 2. The symmetric even/odd splitting (rx_even, rx_odd, ry_even, ry_odd, rz_even, rz_odd)   │
│                          │ creates 6 unique parameters per block, which is double the seed's 3 parameters.           │
│                          │ 3. The seed baseline achieves better accuracy with shared parameters (ry_init, rz_main,   │
│                          │ cry_nnn, ry_final = 4 params, but cry_nnn is shared across 8 gates).                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Proposed improvement:                                                                     │
│                          │ Insert a shared mid-block RY layer between Layer 5 (RZ rotations) and Layer 6 (long-range │
│                          │ CRY entanglers). This adds a single shared "ry_mid" parameter that:                       │
│                          │ - Provides an additional global rotation probe before the long-range entanglement         │
│                          │ - Maintains parameter efficiency (only +1 param per block)                                │
│                          │ - Tests if this extra degree of freedom improves expressivity without excessive           │
│                          │ overfitting                                                                               │
│                          │ - Follows the principle that shared parameters work better than per-qubit parameters for  │
│                          │ this task                                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This change reduces the parameter count from 50 to 42 (adding 1 shared param per block: 1 │
│                          │ × 3 uploads × 2 repeats = 6 circuit params + 2 readout = 50 total, but we're replacing    │
│                          │ some inefficient structure) while potentially improving accuracy through better           │
│                          │ expressivity.                                                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Actually, simpler approach: just add the ry_mid layer with shared parameter. This adds 6  │
│                          │ circuit params (1 param × 3 uploads × 2 repeats), bringing total from 50 to 56. But the   │
│                          │ recommendation suggests it should improve enough to offset the slight parameter increase. │
│                          │ However, to stay competitive, we should also consider removing one of the inefficient     │
│                          │ symmetric parameter splits.                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Best approach: Add ry_mid between Layer 5 and Layer 6 as recommended. This tests the      │
│                          │ hypothesis that an additional global probe before long-range entanglement improves        │
│                          │ learning dynamics.                                                                        │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
