│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ per_qubit_rotations_lean_ansatz                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ The current program achieves 0.91 accuracy but with slower convergence (450 steps)        │
│                          │ compared to earlier variants (180-270 steps). The issue is excessive parameter sharing in │
│                          │ single-qubit rotations combined with a deep circuit.                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit replaces the heavily-shared single-qubit rotations (ry_init, rz_main, ry_final  │
│                          │ all shared across 8 qubits) with per-qubit independent parameters. This allows each qubit │
│                          │ to learn its own optimal rotation angles rather than forcing all qubits to use the same   │
│                          │ angle.                                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Benefits:                                                                                 │
│                          │ - Each qubit can adapt independently to its role in the circuit                           │
│                          │ - Faster convergence by reducing parameter coupling                                       │
│                          │ - Better expressiveness without significantly increasing total params (trades 3 shared    │
│                          │ params for 24 independent ones, but removes redundancy)                                   │
│                          │ - Maintains the proven entanglement structure (CZ rings + CRY layers)                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The total parameter count increases from 4 unique params to 17 unique params per block    │
│                          │ (still modest), but the per-qubit adaptation should accelerate learning and improve       │
│                          │ generalization.                                                                           │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
