╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_crz_diagonal_layer                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz achieves 0.91 test accuracy with only 4 unique parameters per block    │
│                          │ (ry_basis, cry_nnn, rz_readout, plus 2 readout params). Analysis of prior successful      │
│                          │ programs reveals:                                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Prior program 2** achieved the same 0.91 combined score but with 5 parameters per    │
│                          │ block, and critically—it included **parametrized two-qubit diagonal gates** (the CRY      │
│                          │ gates at nearest-neighbor spacing in Layer 5a plus next-nearest-neighbor in Layer 5b).    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Key insight**: The recommendation explicitly suggests turning fixed diagonal CZ      │
│                          │ gates into parametrized CRZ gates. The current program has a fixed nearest-neighbor CZ    │
│                          │ ring (Layer 2) that could be made trainable.                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Cost-benefit**: Replacing the 8 fixed CZ gates in Layer 2 with parametrized          │
│                          │ CRZ(crz_diag) gates adds only **one new parameter** to PARAMETER_KEYS_PER_BLOCK (crz_diag │
│                          │ is fully shared), increasing N_PARAMS from 20 to 22 total. This is a +10% parameter       │
│                          │ increase but should improve expressivity significantly.                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 4. **Rationale**:                                                                         │
│                          │    - Fixed CZ gates provide only fixed entanglement structure; parametrization allows the │
│                          │ circuit to learn the strength and phase of mid-block entanglement.                        │
│                          │    - The nearest-neighbor ring is a critical structural element; making it tunable        │
│                          │ mirrors the success of the CRY layers in prior programs.                                  │
│                          │    - Full parameter sharing across all 8 CRZ gates minimizes overhead while maximizing    │
│                          │ learned connectivity.                                                                     │
│                          │    - This change improves circuit expressivity with minimal complexity, following the     │
│                          │ proven pattern of prior successful designs.                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Expected outcomes**:                                                                    │
│                          │ - Potential gain in test accuracy (0.91 → 0.92+) from richer mid-block entanglement       │
│                          │ - Improved parameter efficiency despite +2 params (test_acc / n_params ratio may improve) │
│                          │ - Faster convergence due to more flexible entanglement structure                          │
│                          │ - Minimal increase in circuit depth (CRZ replaces CZ, same 1-qubit depth per gate)        │
