│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ enhanced_parametrized_entanglement                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ The current ANSATZ_SPEC achieves 0.93 test accuracy with 26 parameters and convergence at │
│                          │ 270 steps. To improve convergence speed and potentially boost accuracy, I propose         │
│                          │ enriching the parametrized entanglement layer by adding nearest-neighbor CRY gates in     │
│                          │ addition to the existing next-nearest-neighbor CRY gates.                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Rationale:**                                                                            │
│                          │ - **Richer adaptive entanglement:** Adding nearest-neighbor CRY gates (which share the    │
│                          │ same parameter "cry_nnn") provides additional flexible entanglement channels without      │
│                          │ increasing the parameter count.                                                           │
│                          │ - **Better feature interaction:** The combination of nearest-neighbor and                 │
│                          │ next-nearest-neighbor parametrized gates creates a denser entanglement graph, allowing    │
│                          │ the optimizer to explore richer quantum state transformations.                            │
│                          │ - **Faster convergence:** More entanglement pathways can accelerate gradient flow and     │
│                          │ convergence, potentially reducing convergence_step_mean from 270.                         │
│                          │ - **Maintained efficiency:** Parameter sharing keeps N_PARAMS at 26 while increasing      │
│                          │ expressivity through gate count and connectivity.                                         │
│                          │ - **Proven pattern:** The second prior program successfully used both nearest-neighbor    │
│                          │ and next-nearest-neighbor CRY gates with the same parameter, achieving 0.93 test          │
│                          │ accuracy.                                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit adds a new layer (Layer 5a) with nearest-neighbor CRY gates before the existing │
│                          │ next-nearest-neighbor CRY layer (Layer 5b), creating a more connected parametrized        │
│                          │ entanglement block.                                                                       │
