│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ enhance_entanglement_depth                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ The current program achieves 0.91 combined score with only 3 unique parameters (ry_basis, │
│                          │ cry_nnn, rz_readout) per block, resulting in 20 total parameters. Prior high-performing   │
│                          │ candidates (0.93 test accuracy) used 4 unique parameters per block (26 total), with       │
│                          │ richer entanglement structures including both nearest-neighbor and next-nearest-neighbor  │
│                          │ CRY gates.                                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The current ANSATZ_SPEC is too compact. It has:                                           │
│                          │ - Layer 1: RY (shared across all qubits)                                                  │
│                          │ - Layer 2: Fixed CZ ring                                                                  │
│                          │ - Layer 3: CRY ring (shared parameter)                                                    │
│                          │ - Layer 4: RZ (shared across all qubits)                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This lacks the depth and expressivity of prior successful designs. The improvement adds:  │
│                          │ 1. An additional parametrized layer of next-nearest-neighbor CRY gates (reusing the       │
│                          │ cry_nnn parameter for efficiency, similar to prior designs)                               │
│                          │ 2. This increases expressivity without adding new unique parameters, leveraging the same  │
│                          │ cry_nnn parameter across both nearest-neighbor and next-nearest-neighbor connectivity     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This mirrors the structure of the second prior program which had both nearest-neighbor    │
│                          │ and next-nearest-neighbor CRY layers sharing the same parameter, achieving 0.93 test      │
│                          │ accuracy with 26 parameters and 196 depth.                                                │
