│ patch_description        │ The current design (score 0.90) achieves 91% test accuracy with 4 parameters per block,   │
│                          │ but shows room for improvement compared to prior programs (score 0.91) that maintained    │
│                          │ similar accuracy with richer entanglement structures.                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Key observation:** The prior high-performing program (second example) used both         │
│                          │ nearest-neighbor CRY and next-nearest-neighbor CRY with full parameter sharing, achieving │
│                          │ test accuracy 0.93 while keeping n_params at 26. The current design has replaced fixed CZ │
│                          │ layers with parametrized CRZ but lost the next-nearest-neighbor connectivity that         │
│                          │ provided expressivity.                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Proposed improvement:** Add a next-nearest-neighbor CRZ layer to inject long-range      │
│                          │ entanglement. By reusing the same `crz_diag` parameter (which already exists), we add 8   │
│                          │ gates with **zero additional parameters**. This mirrors the successful pattern from the   │
│                          │ prior program while maintaining parameter efficiency.                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Why this works:**                                                                       │
│                          │ - Long-range entanglement (diagonal interactions 2 qubits apart) is known to improve      │
│                          │ trainability and expressivity in quantum circuits                                         │
│                          │ - Parameter sharing keeps overhead minimal (N_PARAMS_PER_BLOCK stays at 4)                │
│                          │ - The next-nearest-neighbor structure complements the nearest-neighbor CRZ by creating a  │
│                          │ denser interaction graph                                                                  │
│                          │ - Convergence should remain fast due to low parameter count                               │
│                          │ - This addresses the 2% gap in test accuracy (0.91 → 0.93 in prior work)                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Expected gains:**                                                                       │
│                          │ - Improved test accuracy (+1-2%)                                                          │
│                          │ - Maintained or improved generalization (richer feature maps often reduce overfitting     │
│                          │ when properly regularized)                                                                │
│                          │ - No increase in parameter count or significant depth overhead                            │
│                          │ - Faster convergence due to well-structured entanglement pattern                          │
