│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ reduce_overfitting_via_regularization_gates                                               │
│ patch_description        │ The current program shows significant overfitting: train_accuracy=0.94 but                │
│                          │ test_accuracy=0.90 (gap of 0.04), and it has 32 parameters with lower test accuracy than  │
│                          │ the seed program (26 params, 0.93 test accuracy).                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Root cause analysis:**                                                                  │
│                          │ - The current ansatz has parametrized CRZ gates in Layer 3 (cross-ring entanglement)      │
│                          │ which adds 4 new parameters                                                               │
│                          │ - This increased expressivity without corresponding regularization leads to overfitting   │
│                          │ - The prior seed program (score 0.92) used fixed CZ gates instead, achieving better       │
│                          │ generalization                                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Proposed fix:**                                                                         │
│                          │ Replace the parametrized CRZ gates (Layer 3) with fixed CZ gates, reverting to the proven │
│                          │ structure from the high-scoring seed program. This:                                       │
│                          │ 1. Reduces parameters from 32 to 26 (matching the better seed)                            │
│                          │ 2. Removes unnecessary expressivity that causes overfitting                               │
│                          │ 3. Maintains the beneficial nearest-neighbor and next-nearest-neighbor entanglement       │
│                          │ structure                                                                                 │
│                          │ 4. Should improve test accuracy and reduce the train-test gap                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The key insight is that the parametrized cross-ring entanglement (CRZ) is not helping—the │
│                          │ fixed CZ structure was better. By removing this, we get back to the proven architecture.  │
