╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ reduce_params_improve_structure                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ The current program has 56 parameters (vs. 26 in the best prior), leading to poor         │
│                          │ parameter efficiency (0.02 vs. 0.04) and lower combined score (0.89 vs. 0.92). The issue  │
│                          │ is parameter over-proliferation without corresponding accuracy gains.                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Analysis of prior successes:                                                              │
│                          │ - Best program (score 0.92): 26 params, uses full parameter sharing (ry_init, rz_main,    │
│                          │ ry_final) and efficient entanglement (CZ ring + cross-ring + shared CRY)                  │
│                          │ - Second program (score 0.92): 26 params, adds enrichment layer with parameter reuse (no  │
│                          │ extra params)                                                                             │
│                          │ - Current program (score 0.89): 56 params, uses separate even/odd parameters (rx_even,    │
│                          │ rx_odd, ry_even, ry_odd, rz_even, rz_odd, cry_nn, ry_mid, cry_lr)                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The current design splits parameters unnecessarily (even/odd qubit pairs) without         │
│                          │ demonstrating accuracy improvement. This increases circuit complexity and parameter count │
│                          │ without benefit.                                                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Strategy: Return to the proven high-parameter-sharing structure from the best program,    │
│                          │ but incorporate insights from the current program's entanglement patterns. Specifically:  │
│                          │ 1. Use full parameter sharing for single-qubit rotations (ry_init, rz_main, ry_final) -   │
│                          │ proven efficient                                                                          │
│                          │ 2. Keep nearest-neighbor CRY (cry_nn) for local entanglement                              │
│                          │ 3. Add long-range CRY gates (cry_lr) for global correlation capture                       │
│                          │ 4. Remove the even/odd split and ry_mid layer that inflate parameters without proven      │
│                          │ benefit                                                                                   │
│                          │ 5. Maintain fixed CZ gates for structure                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This reduces parameters from 56 to 26 (matching best prior), improves parameter           │
│                          │ efficiency, and preserves the entanglement diversity that helped the current program's    │
│                          │ validation accuracy.                                                                      │
