                        Patch Metadata - Gen 57/100 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ decouple_cry_entanglement                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ The current program uses a single parameter `cry_nnn` for all 8 next-nearest-neighbor CRY │
│                          │ gates. The prior recommendation suggests decoupling nearest-neighbor and                  │
│                          │ next-nearest-neighbor entanglement by introducing two separate keys: `cry_nn` for         │
│                          │ nearest-neighbor CRY gates and `cry_nnn` for next-nearest-neighbor CRY gates.             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This change adds only one extra parameter per block (from 4 to 5 parameters: ry_init,     │
│                          │ rz_main, cry_nn, cry_nnn, ry_final), which is well within the acceptable range (prior     │
│                          │ runs show combined ≥0.92 with up to ~32 total parameters). The benefit is that the        │
│                          │ optimizer can now independently tune the strength of short-range (nearest-neighbor) vs.   │
│                          │ long-range (next-nearest-neighbor) coupling, rather than forcing them to share the same   │
│                          │ rotation angle.                                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Looking at the prior programs:                                                            │
│                          │ - First program (score 0.91): 32 params, used cry_nn and cry_nnn separately with 8 NN and │
│                          │ 8 NNN gates                                                                               │
│                          │ - Second program (score 0.92): 26 params, collapsed all CRY gates to use cry_nnn only     │
│                          │ - Current program (score 0.91): 26 params, also uses cry_nnn only                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The hypothesis is that re-introducing the separate cry_nn parameter will allow finer      │
│                          │ control over entanglement patterns and improve the combined score back toward 0.92 or     │
│                          │ higher, while keeping parameter count reasonable at 30 total (5 per block × 3 uploads × 2 │
│                          │ repeats + 2 readout).                                                                     │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0276                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
│ model_name               │ openrouter/anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5                                                     │
