╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ upload_scaling_amplitudes                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ The prior programs show strong performance (0.91–0.92 combined scores) but there is       │
│                          │ opportunity to improve validation accuracy and reduce the train-test gap further. The     │
│                          │ recommendation to introduce per-upload amplitude scalars (lambda parameters) is           │
│                          │ theoretically well-motivated: each feature-map/upload cycle encodes increasingly refined  │
│                          │ information from data re-uploading, yet currently all variational blocks apply uniform    │
│                          │ parameter magnitudes across uploads.                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ By introducing three learnable scalars (lambda_0, lambda_1, lambda_2)—one per upload—that │
│                          │ multiplicatively scale all block parameters within each upload cycle, we enable the       │
│                          │ optimizer to dynamically weight early vs. late blocks. Early uploads may benefit from     │
│                          │ smaller amplitudes to avoid rapid saturation, while later uploads can apply stronger      │
│                          │ corrections. This is a lightweight mechanism (only 3 extra parameters) that preserves the │
│                          │ ansatz structure and leverages the natural phase structure of data re-uploading.          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Implementation strategy:                                                                  │
│                          │ 1. Modify ANSATZ_SPEC to include three scaling parameters at the beginning: lambda_0,     │
│                          │ lambda_1, lambda_2.                                                                       │
│                          │ 2. These are "virtual" parameters that will gate all subsequent rotations per upload      │
│                          │ through multiplicative scaling logic in apply_ansatz_block.                               │
│                          │ 3. The approach stays within EVOLVE-BLOCK by using parameter reuse and structural         │
│                          │ innovation within the spec itself.                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Since we can only edit within EVOLVE-BLOCK, we will introduce three independent RY gates  │
│                          │ with unique parameter keys at the start of ANSATZ_SPEC that serve as amplitude scalars.   │
│                          │ Then in the rest of the circuit, we reuse the same parameter names to create              │
│                          │ amplitude-scaled variants of the main circuit.                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ However, a cleaner approach within constraints: introduce three "dummy" single-qubit RY   │
│                          │ rotations using lambda parameters early on, which the optimizer can learn to use as       │
│                          │ scaling factors through the circuit structure. We also strategically reuse these lambda   │
│                          │ parameters on multiple gates to create the scaling effect.                                │
