                        Patch Metadata - Gen 64/100 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ rx_symmetry_breaker                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ The current program achieves a combined score of 0.92 with good validation accuracy       │
│                          │ (0.94) but shows a larger generalization gap (0.03) and slower convergence (360 steps)    │
│                          │ compared to the prior programs (0.92 score, 0.01 gap, 150 steps). The prior programs that │
│                          │ achieved 0.92 used more parameters (32 vs 20) and deeper circuits, suggesting that        │
│                          │ additional learnable parameters and structural diversity can improve both convergence     │
│                          │ speed and generalization.                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Following the formal recommendation, I will add a shared RX rotation layer ("rx_main")    │
│                          │ immediately after the RZ readout layer in each block. This introduces:                    │
│                          │ 1. **Symmetry breaking**: RX rotations in the X basis complement the Y and Z rotations    │
│                          │ already present, breaking symmetries that can lead to barren plateaus.                    │
│                          │ 2. **Increased expressivity**: Adding one more parameter per block (from 3 to 4) allows   │
│                          │ richer state transformations without excessive overhead.                                  │
│                          │ 3. **Proven structure**: Single-qubit rotation sandwiches around entanglers have been     │
│                          │ shown to lift barren plateaus and improve optimization landscape.                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The new structure will be:                                                                │
│                          │ - RY basis rotation (shared)                                                              │
│                          │ - Fixed nearest-neighbor CZ ring                                                          │
│                          │ - Parametrized nearest-neighbor CRY (shared)                                              │
│                          │ - Parametrized next-nearest-neighbor CRY (shared)                                         │
│                          │ - RZ readout (shared)                                                                     │
│                          │ - **NEW: RX main layer (shared)** ← breaks symmetry, improves convergence                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This increases N_PARAMS_PER_BLOCK from 3 to 4, leading to N_PARAMS = 26 (up from 20),     │
│                          │ which aligns with the prior successful programs' parameter counts and should improve both │
│                          │ convergence speed and generalization gap.                                                 │
