                        Patch Metadata - Gen 65/100 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ adaptive_block_scaling_ansatz                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ The current program achieves 0.88 combined score with an overly restrictive "information  │
│                          │ bottleneck" design (single CRY gate) that limits expressiveness. Prior programs achieved  │
│                          │ 0.92 by using richer entanglement structures with multiple parametrized two-qubit gates   │
│                          │ at different ranges.                                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This new approach introduces **adaptive per-upload block scaling** combined with a **more │
│                          │ expressive ansatz architecture**. Instead of a single bottleneck gate, we use:            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Dual-range entanglement**: Nearest-neighbor CRY gates (local correlations) plus      │
│                          │ next-nearest-neighbor CRY gates (longer-range structure), both with independent           │
│                          │ parameters.                                                                               │
│                          │ 2. **Three upload-level scaling factors** (lambda_0, lambda_1, lambda_2) that modulate    │
│                          │ all block parameters within each feature-map/upload cycle. This lightweight mechanism     │
│                          │ (only 3 extra parameters) allows the optimizer to dynamically weight early vs. late       │
│                          │ variational blocks, improving convergence and test accuracy.                              │
│                          │ 3. **Readout preparation layer**: Final RZ rotations on all qubits to prepare the         │
│                          │ measurement basis.                                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The adaptive scaling echoes successful role-based block weighting from prior searches and │
│                          │ should sharpen convergence while maintaining parameter efficiency. The richer             │
│                          │ entanglement structure (comparable to the 0.92 baseline) combined with adaptive scaling   │
│                          │ should recover and exceed the prior performance.                                          │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0531                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
│ model_name               │ openrouter/anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5                                                     │
│ temperature              │ 1.0                                                                                       │
│ max_output_tokens        │ 16384                                                                                     │
