│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ rx_symmetry_breaker_after_rz                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ The current program achieves a combined score of 0.90 with test accuracy of 0.90. The     │
│                          │ prior programs show that adding a shared RX symmetry-breaker layer can improve            │
│                          │ performance. The second prior program (score 0.92) uses 5 parameters per block and        │
│                          │ achieves better test accuracy (0.93) with lower generalization gap (0.01).                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The key insight is that the current program has only 4 unique parameters per block        │
│                          │ (ry_init, crz_cr, rz_main, cry_nnn, ry_final), but the RZ layer followed by RY creates a  │
│                          │ potential symmetry constraint. By inserting a shared RX layer immediately after the RZ    │
│                          │ main layer, we can:                                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Break symmetries that constrain gradient flow                                          │
│                          │ 2. Add expressiveness without excessive parameter growth (only 1 new parameter)           │
│                          │ 3. Improve the ability to learn complex decision boundaries                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This follows the recommendation that "Single-parameter RX sandwiches around the CRY       │
│                          │ entanglers have lifted symmetry constraints in prior searches and may push the combined   │
│                          │ score past 0.92 by improving gradient flow."                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The modification inserts 8 RX gates (all sharing the same parameter "rx_main")            │
│                          │ immediately after the 8 RZ gates in Layer 4, before the CRY entanglers in Layer 5. This   │
│                          │ creates a rotation-based symmetry breaker that helps the optimizer escape local minima    │
│                          │ and improves gradient flow through the circuit.                                           │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0257                                                                                   │
