                        Patch Metadata - Gen 70/100 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ rx_symmetry_breaker_after_rz                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ The current program achieves a combined score of 0.91 with 32 parameters. The prior       │
│                          │ recommendation suggests that adding a shared RX symmetry-breaker layer immediately after  │
│                          │ the RZ main layer can improve gradient flow and lift symmetry constraints that may be     │
│                          │ limiting optimization.                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Analysis of the current architecture:                                                     │
│                          │ - The current ANSATZ_SPEC has RZ gates with full parameter sharing (rz_main), followed by │
│                          │ CRY entanglers                                                                            │
│                          │ - The prior programs show that introducing an RX layer after RZ can break symmetries that │
│                          │ prevent the optimizer from exploring the full parameter space                             │
│                          │ - The second prior program (score 0.92) uses 32 parameters and achieves better test       │
│                          │ accuracy (0.93 vs 0.93 in current, but with better validation accuracy 0.93 vs 0.92)      │
│                          │ - Adding a single shared RX parameter after the RZ layer maintains parameter efficiency   │
│                          │ while improving expressivity                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The modification:                                                                         │
│                          │ 1. Insert eight RX gates (one per qubit) immediately after the eight RZ gates in Layer 4  │
│                          │ 2. All RX gates share a single parameter "rx_main" for efficiency                         │
│                          │ 3. Add "rx_main" to the parameter keys list (it will be automatically ordered by the      │
│                          │ validator)                                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This approach:                                                                            │
│                          │ - Maintains the same parameter count (still 5 unique parameters per block: ry_init,       │
│                          │ rz_main, rx_main, cry_nn, cry_nnn)                                                        │
│                          │ - Improves gradient flow by breaking the symmetry between RZ and the following CRY layers │
│                          │ - Follows the proven pattern from prior successful searches                               │
│                          │ - Requires minimal code change with high expected impact                                  │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0264                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
