│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ consolidate_boundary_ry_layers                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ The current program has two separate boundary RY layers (ry_init and ry_final), each      │
│                          │ consuming 8 parameter slots per block. By consolidating these into a single shared        │
│                          │ parameter "ry_bound", we reduce N_PARAMS_PER_BLOCK from 6 to 5 (from 38 total to 32 total │
│                          │ circuit params), freeing one parameter slot while maintaining expressivity.               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This consolidation:                                                                       │
│                          │ 1. Reduces parameter count from 38 to 32 (N_PARAMS from 38 to 32), improving parameter    │
│                          │ efficiency                                                                                │
│                          │ 2. Maintains the same circuit depth and gate count since we're only changing parameter    │
│                          │ sharing, not the gate structure                                                           │
│                          │ 3. Keeps all 6 unique parameter keys (ry_bound, rz_main, rx_main, cry_nn, cry_nnn, plus   │
│                          │ one slot for future expansion)                                                            │
│                          │ 4. Aligns with the second prior program's philosophy of aggressive parameter sharing for  │
│                          │ better generalization                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The recommendation explicitly suggests this change, and the prior program with score 0.92 │
│                          │ (second one) demonstrates that aggressive parameter sharing can achieve high accuracy     │
│                          │ with minimal parameters (20 params vs current 38).                                        │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0262                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
