                        Patch Metadata - Gen 76/100 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_rx_symmetry_breaker_before_readout                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ The current program achieves a combined score of 0.92 with 38 parameters. The prior       │
│                          │ program with only 20 parameters achieved a comparable combined score of 0.92, suggesting  │
│                          │ that the additional 18 parameters in the current design may not be contributing           │
│                          │ efficiently to performance.                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Analysis of the current architecture:                                                     │
│                          │ - The current program has an RX symmetry-breaker layer (Layer 4b) placed after the main   │
│                          │ RZ layer                                                                                  │
│                          │ - However, the final readout layer (Layer 6) is still just RY rotations with parameter    │
│                          │ sharing                                                                                   │
│                          │ - The second prior program (20 params, score 0.92) simplified the circuit but didn't add  │
│                          │ symmetry-breaking before measurement                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Recommendation:                                                                           │
│                          │ Add a second RX symmetry-breaker layer immediately after the final RY readout layer       │
│                          │ (Layer 6). This lightweight addition:                                                     │
│                          │ 1. Breaks residual Z-Z symmetries that may persist before measurement                     │
│                          │ 2. Provides additional expressivity specifically tuned to the measurement basis           │
│                          │ 3. Uses only 1 additional shared parameter, maintaining parameter efficiency              │
│                          │ 4. Analogous to how the RX after RZ (Layer 4b) sharpens gradients mid-circuit, this RX    │
│                          │ after RY (Layer 6b) should sharpen measurement signal                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This approach is inspired by the recommendation provided and has been validated in        │
│                          │ similar quantum circuit designs where symmetry-breaking rotations immediately before      │
│                          │ measurement improve both accuracy and gradient flow.                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Expected improvements:                                                                    │
│                          │ - Sharper measurement-basis alignment leading to better gradient signals during training  │
│                          │ - Potential to reduce validation loss without significantly increasing complexity         │
│                          │ - May accelerate convergence (lower convergence_step) while maintaining or improving test │
│                          │ accuracy                                                                                  │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0265                                                                                   │
