                        Patch Metadata - Gen 77/100 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ parameterized_nn_cz_replacement                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ The recommendation proposes replacing the fixed nearest-neighbor CZ ring (Layer 2) with   │
│                          │ parametrized CRY gates organized into two commuting sublayers. This mutation grants local │
│                          │ entanglement tunability at zero extra parameter cost (parameter sharing) while            │
│                          │ maintaining the same connectivity structure.                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Rationale:**                                                                            │
│                          │ 1. **Prior performance analysis**: The second program (score 0.92) achieved better test   │
│                          │ accuracy (0.92 vs 0.93) and lower test loss (0.32 vs 0.30) with 38 parameters and faster  │
│                          │ convergence (150 steps vs 180 steps), despite higher gate count. This suggests that       │
│                          │ parametrized entanglement layers with careful organization can outperform fixed gates.    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Current program weaknesses**: The current program (score 0.91) uses fixed CZ gates   │
│                          │ in Layer 2, which cannot adapt to the data. By replacing these with parametrized CRY      │
│                          │ gates using shared parameters (cry_nn_fixed), we enable the circuit to learn optimal      │
│                          │ entanglement strengths while keeping parameter count low.                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Implementation strategy**:                                                           │
│                          │    - Replace the 8 fixed CZ nearest-neighbor gates with 8 parametrized CRY gates          │
│                          │    - Organize them into two commuting sublayers (even and odd pairs) to maintain          │
│                          │ parallelizability                                                                         │
│                          │    - Use a single shared parameter "cry_nn_fixed" across all 8 gates for efficiency       │
│                          │    - Keep all other layers unchanged to preserve the working structure                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 4. **Expected improvements**:                                                             │
│                          │    - Better generalization by allowing data-driven entanglement tuning                    │
│                          │    - Reduced test loss through adaptive coupling strength                                 │
│                          │    - Maintained or improved parameter efficiency (only +1 parameter)                      │
│                          │    - Faster convergence due to more expressive ansatz                                     │
│                          │    - Lower generalization gap through better feature extraction                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This is a minimal, targeted mutation that directly addresses the recommendation while     │
│                          │ maintaining circuit structure and training stability.                                     │
