│ patch_name               │ hybrid_efficient_ansatz                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ This crossover combines the best aspects of three high-performing candidates:             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Current program (score 0.92)**: Minimal parameter count (20 params), fast            │
│                          │ convergence (360 steps), but suboptimal test accuracy (0.92) and higher test loss (0.35). │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **First prior program (score 0.91)**: More expressive with 32 params, excellent        │
│                          │ generalization gap (0.02), balanced accuracies (train 0.94, test 0.93).                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Second prior program (score 0.92)**: 38 params, best validation accuracy (0.94),     │
│                          │ lowest validation loss (0.30), fastest convergence (150 steps), but slightly higher test  │
│                          │ loss (0.32).                                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Crossover strategy:**                                                                   │
│                          │ - Start with the efficient parametrization of the current program (3 independent          │
│                          │ parameters: ry_basis, cry_nnn, rz_readout) which achieves low parameter count             │
│                          │ - Add the symmetric RX layer from the second prior program to break symmetries and        │
│                          │ improve expressiveness (adding rx_readout parameter)                                      │
│                          │ - Preserve the nearest-neighbor CZ ring for local entanglement (from all programs)        │
│                          │ - Add diagonal CZ coupling (from first prior) for long-range correlations                 │
│                          │ - Use parallelized two-qubit gate structure (from first prior) to maintain efficiency     │
│                          │ while enabling richer entanglement patterns                                               │
│                          │ - Keep the simple 3-parameter structure but strategically place gates to maximize         │
│                          │ expressiveness                                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Expected improvements:**                                                                │
│                          │ - Better test accuracy through richer entanglement without parameter explosion            │
│                          │ - Faster convergence through better structured gates                                      │
│                          │ - Lower generalization gap via symmetry-breaking RX layer                                 │
│                          │ - Balanced parameter efficiency (fewer params than second prior, but more expressive than │
│                          │ current)                                                                                  │
